  "method": "pnpm e2e:serve shows the native seat, so the page already has DSH's own Memory System row. The fallback entry mounts only in layouts without that seat, so the check builds the element the fallback builds on the live page: the classes of the loaded Mnemon stylesheet (NS3bAW_entry, _entryIcon, _entryLabel), the shared brain icon at the size the fallback passes (18 on main, 16 with the fix), inserted under New Session as placeEntry does. Values are getComputedStyle and getBoundingClientRect with every row present; iconLeft and labelLeft are relative to the sidebar column. \"open\" selects the native Memory System row and marks the fallback as the fallback marks itself. The screenshots hide the native Memory System row, so each shows one Memory System entry beside Plugins, as a fallback layout does.",
